I sit on the bed.
I take my mobile phone.
It is evening in Berlin.
In Mexico it is morning.
I call my parents.
My mother is on the phone.
She asks, "Maya, are you in Berlin?"
I laugh.
"Yes, Mama, I am here," I say.
My father is also on the phone.
He asks, "How is the room?"
I answer, "It is very nice."
"Is there a bed?" he asks.
"Yes, there is a bed and a table," I say.
"Is it very cold?" my mother asks.
"Yes, but my room is warm," I say cheerfully.
"I am fine."
"Everything is okay."
I hear our dog Lola.
I smile.
I am tired, but I am happy.
